gbench fix for BenchFlow 0.6.3's docker sandbox, applied by gbench/docker/skillsbench.Dockerfile
to the orchestrator's environment (/app/skillsbench/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages). Paths are
relative to that directory.

benchflow/sandbox/docker.py: BenchFlow retries a task environment's `docker compose build` twice
(2 s, then 5 s later) when the failure matches _DOCKER_BUILD_RETRYABLE_ERRORS, its list of
transient build failures (apt signature errors, no space left, read/connection timeouts). The
list did not include a failure of the Docker daemon's containerd image store while it commits a
layer:

  failed to export layer: CreateDiff: mount callback failed on ...: failed to commit: rename
  /var/lib/containerd/io.containerd.content.v1.content/ingest/<ref>/data
  /var/lib/containerd/io.containerd.content.v1.content/blobs/sha256/<digest>: no such file or
  directory

On 2026-10-13 (gbench validation run pool-10-13-003542) the task lab-unit-harmonization failed
this way in step 4/7 (`pip install`, whose output ends "Successfully installed ..."), after 78 s
and before the agent started (0 tool calls, 0 tokens, empty trajectory); BenchFlow classified the
error "other", ran no verifier and wrote no reward. The same Dockerfile built and was scored on
2026-10-10 and 2026-10-11. The patch adds that failure to the list, so the build is retried like
the other transient failures; any other build failure still fails the trial at once, and a third
failure of this kind still fails it. The launcher records each retry (sandbox_build_retries).

--- a/benchflow/sandbox/docker.py
+++ b/benchflow/sandbox/docker.py
@@ -51,6 +51,18 @@
     re.compile(r"readtimeouterror", re.IGNORECASE),
     re.compile(r"read timed out", re.IGNORECASE),
     re.compile(r"connection (?:timed out|reset by peer)", re.IGNORECASE),
+    # gbench (skillsbench_benchflow_build_retry.patch): the Docker daemon's containerd image
+    # store lost a layer while committing it ("failed to export layer ... failed to commit:
+    # rename .../ingest/<ref>/data .../blobs/sha256/<digest>: no such file or directory"): a
+    # failure of the daemon's content store after the step's command had finished (2026-10-13
+    # gbench run, lab-unit-harmonization, step 4/7 `pip install`; the same Dockerfile built on
+    # 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-11). The agent has not started when the build runs.
+    re.compile(
+        r"failed to export layer\b.*?failed to commit: rename \S*"
+        r"io\.containerd\.content\.v1\.content/ingest/\S+ \S*"
+        r"io\.containerd\.content\.v1\.content/blobs/\S+: no such file or directory",
+        re.IGNORECASE | re.DOTALL,
+    ),
 )
 
 # Compose-up network-race retry config lives in _compose so the host docker
